# Plugin Architecture: Subprocess-Based CLAP Hosting

## Core Design Principles

Sonara uses **subprocess isolation** for CLAP plugins to achieve crash isolation, GUI support, and security. Each plugin runs in its own process with IPC (Inter-Process Communication).

**Key Benefits**: Crash isolation, independent GUI event loop, security sandboxing
**Key Tradeoff**: 6-20ms added latency, memory overhead per plugin
**Reference**: PLUGIN_ARCHITECTURE.md for comprehensive technical details

## Architecture Overview

```
Engine Process                        Plugin Subprocess
┌──────────────────┐                ┌──────────────────┐
│ AudioDevice API  │                │ CLAP Plugin      │
│ ↓                │                │ ↑                │
│ Shared Memory    │◄──IPC Socket──►│ Event Loop       │
│ Ring Buffers     │                │ GUI Callbacks    │
└──────────────────┘                └──────────────────┘
  Audio Thread                         Plugin Thread
```

